dist
build

# Environment files
# A pattern without `**` is matched against the path relative to the context
# root only, so a bare `.env` excludes ./.env and nothing else. That is not
# enough here: the build context is the repo root (`context: .`, `file:
# ./Dockerfile`) and stage 5 copies the API tree wholesale with
# `COPY ./apps/api ./`, so apps/api/.env — which holds
# LEARNHOUSE_AUTH_JWT_SECRET_KEY and the database connection string — would be
# baked into the published image at /app/api/.env. apps/api/.dockerignore does
# not help: Docker reads the ignore file next to the context root, and that one
# only applies when the context is ./apps/api.
#
# CI never hits this (checkout is a clean clone and .env is untracked), but a
# local `docker build .` at the repo root does. Match at every depth instead.
**/.env
**/.env.*

